From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:26:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: release PPE tables on remove

The controller-wide PPE flow table and each PPE's L2 flow table remain
allocated when the Ethernet platform driver is removed.

"net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: fix mtk_eth_offload_init memory leak" creates
the shared flow table once and destroys it on the probe error path,
separately from the per-PPE cleanup.  Preserve that ordering on the
successful remove path: unregister the netdevs first, then destroy the
shared flow table and, through mtk_ppe_deinit(), the per-PPE tables,
exactly once.

MediaTek's patch destroys the shared flow table in mtk_ppe_deinit(), which
is also reached on the probe error path before the table exists.  Its
mtk_ppe_offload.c part is in that other patch.

Based-on-patch-by: chak-kei.lam <chak-kei.lam@mediatek.com>
Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/f7eec2ff2e4fc8ded3439d7805c0aaa030ef9e07/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-ppe-33-net-ethernet-mtk_eth_soc-fix-mtk_eth_offload_init-memory-leak.patch
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6078,6 +6078,11 @@ static void mtk_remove(struct platform_d
 
 	mtk_napi_del(eth);
 	mtk_cleanup(eth);
+	if (eth->soc->offload_version) {
+		rhashtable_destroy(&eth->flow_table);
+		mtk_ppe_deinit(eth);
+	}
+
 	free_netdev(eth->dummy_dev);
 	mtk_mdio_cleanup(eth);
 }
